#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""dotgrid-livectl: the one source of truth for the DotGrid Live wallpaper.

Keeps the state (manual pause, mode, bars, fps, elements, speeds) in
~/.config/dotgrid/live.json, computes the automatic pause from power profile,
battery and screen lock, shows a tray icon (StatusNotifierItem), registers the
global shortcut and exports everything on the session bus:

    service org.dotgrid.Live, object /org/dotgrid/Live, interface org.dotgrid.Live
      Status() -> s            full state as JSON
      Pause() / Resume() / Toggle()
      Set(s key, s json) -> s  change one setting, returns "" or an error
      Theme(s day|night|schedule) -> s   switch the whole DotGrid theme
                               (dotgrid-theme / dotgrid-auto); the wallpaper follows
      signal Changed(s json)   after every change, same JSON as Status()

      signal Levels(ay)        external data for the night bars and pipes:
                               [source, 26 bars, 4 pipes], 0..255 each;
                               source 0 none (wallpaper animates on its own),
                               1 audio spectrum, 2 system load

The wallpaper listens to Changed; without this service it falls back to
live.json and its own defaults (no autopause, no audio/system data).
"""
